## Keeping Generated Files Current

Files under `.cursor/rules/` and `.cursor/skills/` are templates from **`ca-ai-tools-setup`**
(`github:mi-examples/ca-ai-tools-setup`, see its `templates/` directory). Re-running the
installer without `--force` does **not** refresh files that already exist, so this repo can
silently fall behind the current template set — missing new rules, stale cross-references,
or superseded conventions.

If a generated file looks outdated — it doesn't reference a rule another current file points
at, or documents a convention a newer file contradicts — treat that as a signal this repo
predates the latest templates: fetch the current version of the affected file(s) from
`github:mi-examples/ca-ai-tools-setup` (local `.cursor/rules/<name>.mdc` maps to
`templates/cursor/rules/<name>.mdc`), update the local file(s) while preserving any
repo-specific customizations, and tell the user what changed and why before it's committed.
Do not blanket-overwrite with `--force` — that also discards intentional per-repo edits.

